@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Why
+
+Some clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch documents rather than JSON Patch. The library has `applyPatch` (RFC 6902) but no way to apply a merge patch.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add and export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`; it returns the merged document.
+- Governing standard: JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (the request cites RFC 7386; that number is the original publication of the same format, and RFC 7396 is the RFC that obsoletes it and is the one named in the project context. The `MergePatch` algorithm is identical).
+- Not breaking: purely additive; no existing export changes.
+- Out of scope: generating a merge patch from two documents, `application/merge-patch+json` media-type handling, JSON text parsing, any change to `applyPatch`/`resolvePointer`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: applying RFC 7396 merge patches to JSON documents without mutating inputs.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts` (new export), `src/index.test.ts` (tests). No dependency or `package.json` changes.
